note twice a second: when the clipboard has changed and Hop is not there to keep the history, this program does
fn ucliptick to void
uindextick
pb = umsg ucl c_pasteboard usl m_general_pasteboard 0 0 0
cc = umsg pb usl m_change_count 0 0 0
if eq cc get g_n 35
ret
end
put g_n 35 cc
if uhoprunning
ret
end
ucliprecord pb
end

note after this program put something on the clipboard itself: that change is not a new copied thing; a text that
note was pasted moves to the front of the history, as in Hop
